{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAxkN6EdBxB8ZLA6Vvqh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KsrEqsBFfoCXUZNsTXfkLa","name":"mcp__ac_review__source_read","input":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"r-prod-1","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"specification/PRODUCT.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[1,60]},"sha256":"9ebc8342affe8c5e0afb08ebe22f3f98f73f7bdc64db00eee17674c47274bef7"},"encoding":"utf8","max_content_bytes":8192}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5306,"cache_read_input_tokens":65689,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5306},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9ee27ae-0996-4105-ba6f-30f3c0f28675","uuid":"7844b742-cc3a-4650-b78e-979f6ea98505","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:26:25.551Z","request_id":"req_011CgAxkMk9vu5Gpfmz7tbaH","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01KsrEqsBFfoCXUZNsTXfkLa":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"r-prod-1","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"specification/PRODUCT.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[1,60]},"sha256":"9ebc8342affe8c5e0afb08ebe22f3f98f73f7bdc64db00eee17674c47274bef7"},"encoding":"utf8","max_content_bytes":8192}}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01KsrEqsBFfoCXUZNsTXfkLa","display_name":"Source Read","server_display_name":"a_c.graphify.fd-support","tool_name":"source.read"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KsrEqsBFfoCXUZNsTXfkLa","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:d7fc791bdd85cb029e14b756ae6c54472fac7b53d0e6f60520feb595cd3b83bb\",\"sha256\":\"d7fc791bdd85cb029e14b756ae6c54472fac7b53d0e6f60520feb595cd3b83bb\"},\"id\":\"r-prod-1\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=5a0d6bd5e7c3cb9be6034296e08aa2516ccd56fb792f49570d98a894912efbc6]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"# Axiomatic Calculus Implementations\\n\\n## Product boundary\\n\\nThis source project constructs implementations of the **axiomatic calculus**,\\n`a_c`, identified by `urn:stdo:concept:axiomatic-calculus:a-c`. Its bounded context\\nis `urn:a-c-implementations:bounded-context:realization`.\\n\\nThe exact selected published STDO `AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md` owns calculus meaning.\\nThe shared requirements here own implementation obligations. A tenant's design\\nowns its computational calculus, representation, operations, concrete stack and\\ndemonstrated fragment. Neither an implementation nor its successful use amends\\nthe calculus or accepts a subject interpretation.\\n\\n## Capability\\n\\nA realization consumes an explicitly authored symbolic model and its exact\\nsignature and basis. It checks a declared structural fragment, preserves the\\nmodel through its representation, and supports source-reenterable inspection\\nand bounded acquisition. It keeps constraints, latitude, residuals, traversals,\\ntransformations and judgments distinguishable from ordinary objects and edges.\\n\\nThe initial Graphify realization carries all eight fundamental record families\\nand their exact content. Its mechanical checks and acquisition operations have\\nan explicitly bounded contract. It does not execute arbitrary predicates,\\ntransform models, select applicable frames, infer logical truth or supply\\nsemantic acceptance. Unsupported operations refuse rather than silently pass.\\n\\nA tenant may also facilitate creation of that model from an exact source\\ncorpus through a declared F_P authoring workflow. Graphify extraction and\\ndiscovery may supply authoring context inside this workflow; an existing\\nnative interpretation is not a prerequisite. The workflow retains exact source\\ngrounding, authoring provenance, coverage dispositions and unresolved meaning.\\nAuthoring, mechanical validation, carrier generation and external semantic\\nassessment remain separate claims. A generated model starts as a proposal.\\n\\nAn unaccepted model may have a clearly identified **proposal view**. That view\\nis not `a_c.X.C` admission. An encoding represented as the calculus's accepted-\\ninterpretation carrier relation requires a separate semantic judgment over the\\nexact unchanged model. Tooling checks the supplied coordinates; decision\\nauthority and semantic fitness remain external judgments. Carrier admission is\\na separate judgment over unchanged carrier bytes; creating bytes or passing a\\npartial check does not itself issue that judgment. Its declared assessment may\\nbe mechanical, as in `F_D[v_carrier_admission]`.\\n\\n## F_D support for F_P development actors\\n\\nThe Product additionally provides deterministic support tools for F_P\\nExecutives, Workers and Reviewers building in a Specification Methodology\\nworkspace. STDO3.0 owns the methodology and consequently the contracts these\\ntools support: lifecycle, role duties, triage/re-entry, frame/activation,\\napplicability, admission, results/conjunction, review/independence and acceptance.\\nThe tools consume those contracts through an exact caller-selected method/profile\\nbinding. a_c owns their supplied inputs, outputs, checked properties, public use\\nand qualification; it does not create a second lifecycle or coordinate F_P work.\\n\\n| Deterministic support | Use by F_P actors |\\n|---|---|\\n| Discover tool contracts; bind/observe exact Product, method and current workspace | Executive, Worker and Reviewer identify supported operations, input identities, current material bytes and explicit unsupported contracts. |\\n| Resolve records/raw source/grounding; query authored dependencies, impact and coverage | All three acquire deciding content and declared relationships. Executive uses them for its selections; Workers inspect the affected implementation/proof; Reviewers acquire source and evidence independently. |\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[1,60]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"9ebc8342affe8c5e0afb08ebe22f3f98f73f7bdc64db00eee17674c47274bef7\",\"selected_sha256\":\"612a22f39d58a8958d4f4d18cf024ba8c09e2afa1a6a618958d1f5a22f029b35\",\"size_bytes\":3814,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"specification/PRODUCT.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1,60]},\"sha256\":\"9ebc8342affe8c5e0afb08ebe22f3f98f73f7bdc64db00eee17674c47274bef7\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9ee27ae-0996-4105-ba6f-30f3c0f28675","uuid":"e5cc5979-b560-4ae1-9f88-f53741d31f2f","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:26:25.994Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:d7fc791bdd85cb029e14b756ae6c54472fac7b53d0e6f60520feb595cd3b83bb\",\"sha256\":\"d7fc791bdd85cb029e14b756ae6c54472fac7b53d0e6f60520feb595cd3b83bb\"},\"id\":\"r-prod-1\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=5a0d6bd5e7c3cb9be6034296e08aa2516ccd56fb792f49570d98a894912efbc6]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"# Axiomatic Calculus Implementations\\n\\n## Product boundary\\n\\nThis source project constructs implementations of the **axiomatic calculus**,\\n`a_c`, identified by `urn:stdo:concept:axiomatic-calculus:a-c`. Its bounded context\\nis `urn:a-c-implementations:bounded-context:realization`.\\n\\nThe exact selected published STDO `AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md` owns calculus meaning.\\nThe shared requirements here own implementation obligations. A tenant's design\\nowns its computational calculus, representation, operations, concrete stack and\\ndemonstrated fragment. Neither an implementation nor its successful use amends\\nthe calculus or accepts a subject interpretation.\\n\\n## Capability\\n\\nA realization consumes an explicitly authored symbolic model and its exact\\nsignature and basis. It checks a declared structural fragment, preserves the\\nmodel through its representation, and supports source-reenterable inspection\\nand bounded acquisition. It keeps constraints, latitude, residuals, traversals,\\ntransformations and judgments distinguishable from ordinary objects and edges.\\n\\nThe initial Graphify realization carries all eight fundamental record families\\nand their exact content. Its mechanical checks and acquisition operations have\\nan explicitly bounded contract. It does not execute arbitrary predicates,\\ntransform models, select applicable frames, infer logical truth or supply\\nsemantic acceptance. Unsupported operations refuse rather than silently pass.\\n\\nA tenant may also facilitate creation of that model from an exact source\\ncorpus through a declared F_P authoring workflow. Graphify extraction and\\ndiscovery may supply authoring context inside this workflow; an existing\\nnative interpretation is not a prerequisite. The workflow retains exact source\\ngrounding, authoring provenance, coverage dispositions and unresolved meaning.\\nAuthoring, mechanical validation, carrier generation and external semantic\\nassessment remain separate claims. A generated model starts as a proposal.\\n\\nAn unaccepted model may have a clearly identified **proposal view**. That view\\nis not `a_c.X.C` admission. An encoding represented as the calculus's accepted-\\ninterpretation carrier relation requires a separate semantic judgment over the\\nexact unchanged model. Tooling checks the supplied coordinates; decision\\nauthority and semantic fitness remain external judgments. Carrier admission is\\na separate judgment over unchanged carrier bytes; creating bytes or passing a\\npartial check does not itself issue that judgment. Its declared assessment may\\nbe mechanical, as in `F_D[v_carrier_admission]`.\\n\\n## F_D support for F_P development actors\\n\\nThe Product additionally provides deterministic support tools for F_P\\nExecutives, Workers and Reviewers building in a Specification Methodology\\nworkspace. STDO3.0 owns the methodology and consequently the contracts these\\ntools support: lifecycle, role duties, triage/re-entry, frame/activation,\\napplicability, admission, results/conjunction, review/independence and acceptance.\\nThe tools consume those contracts through an exact caller-selected method/profile\\nbinding. a_c owns their supplied inputs, outputs, checked properties, public use\\nand qualification; it does not create a second lifecycle or coordinate F_P work.\\n\\n| Deterministic support | Use by F_P actors |\\n|---|---|\\n| Discover tool contracts; bind/observe exact Product, method and current workspace | Executive, Worker and Reviewer identify supported operations, input identities, current material bytes and explicit unsupported contracts. |\\n| Resolve records/raw source/grounding; query authored dependencies, impact and coverage | All three acquire deciding content and declared relationships. Executive uses them for its selections; Workers inspect the affected implementation/proof; Reviewers acquire source and evidence independently. |\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[1,60]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"9ebc8342affe8c5e0afb08ebe22f3f98f73f7bdc64db00eee17674c47274bef7\",\"selected_sha256\":\"612a22f39d58a8958d4f4d18cf024ba8c09e2afa1a6a618958d1f5a22f029b35\",\"size_bytes\":3814,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"specification/PRODUCT.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1,60]},\"sha256\":\"9ebc8342affe8c5e0afb08ebe22f3f98f73f7bdc64db00eee17674c47274bef7\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:d7fc791bdd85cb029e14b756ae6c54472fac7b53d0e6f60520feb595cd3b83bb","sha256":"d7fc791bdd85cb029e14b756ae6c54472fac7b53d0e6f60520feb595cd3b83bb"},"id":"r-prod-1","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=5a0d6bd5e7c3cb9be6034296e08aa2516ccd56fb792f49570d98a894912efbc6]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"# Axiomatic Calculus Implementations\n\n## Product boundary\n\nThis source project constructs implementations of the **axiomatic calculus**,\n`a_c`, identified by `urn:stdo:concept:axiomatic-calculus:a-c`. Its bounded context\nis `urn:a-c-implementations:bounded-context:realization`.\n\nThe exact selected published STDO `AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md` owns calculus meaning.\nThe shared requirements here own implementation obligations. A tenant's design\nowns its computational calculus, representation, operations, concrete stack and\ndemonstrated fragment. Neither an implementation nor its successful use amends\nthe calculus or accepts a subject interpretation.\n\n## Capability\n\nA realization consumes an explicitly authored symbolic model and its exact\nsignature and basis. It checks a declared structural fragment, preserves the\nmodel through its representation, and supports source-reenterable inspection\nand bounded acquisition. It keeps constraints, latitude, residuals, traversals,\ntransformations and judgments distinguishable from ordinary objects and edges.\n\nThe initial Graphify realization carries all eight fundamental record families\nand their exact content. Its mechanical checks and acquisition operations have\nan explicitly bounded contract. It does not execute arbitrary predicates,\ntransform models, select applicable frames, infer logical truth or supply\nsemantic acceptance. Unsupported operations refuse rather than silently pass.\n\nA tenant may also facilitate creation of that model from an exact source\ncorpus through a declared F_P authoring workflow. Graphify extraction and\ndiscovery may supply authoring context inside this workflow; an existing\nnative interpretation is not a prerequisite. The workflow retains exact source\ngrounding, authoring provenance, coverage dispositions and unresolved meaning.\nAuthoring, mechanical validation, carrier generation and external semantic\nassessment remain separate claims. A generated model starts as a proposal.\n\nAn unaccepted model may have a clearly identified **proposal view**. That view\nis not `a_c.X.C` admission. An encoding represented as the calculus's accepted-\ninterpretation carrier relation requires a separate semantic judgment over the\nexact unchanged model. Tooling checks the supplied