{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DWGZeDqC6RvKbsQpvDxLem","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:9c6fa357a6785c2d42508d7f6fa47ccfb9b1f753eaedd64e3bc82629ad7e3491\",\"sha256\":\"9c6fa357a6785c2d42508d7f6fa47ccfb9b1f753eaedd64e3bc82629ad7e3491\"},\"id\":\"r-fdt-1\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=8b58fa747b08b4d8d7aa0fc7d8bfb2f4a4e47e6fa84e7ec659f0e37feb798fc9]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"# Deterministic Support Tools for F_P Actors\\n\\n**Family**: REQ-AC-FD-*\\n**Status**: Deferred\\n**Category**: Capability\\n\\nThis family specifies additional tools supporting F_P Executives, Workers and\\nReviewers. Deferred means owning design and realization are pending; the Product\\noutcome is retained. STDO3.0 owns the methodology and its contracts. The\\n[source-owner map](fd-source-owner-map.md) binds the exact provisional derivation\\nreference and the owner clauses cited below. Runtime use consumes the caller's\\nexact selected method/profile through a declared supported binding, without\\nadopting that provisional candidate or changing a_c's installed builder basis.\\n\\nEvery operation has an exact versioned input/output contract and reproducible\\nchecks over its supplied inputs. External observations retain their identity,\\nscope and time. A named source/carrier/dispatch/write operation is distinct from\\nan `F_D[v]` evaluation/proof returning a judgment; neither makes the invoked\\nF_P operation or its semantic answer deterministic. Existing AC-R-001..015 and\\nthe separate F_P source-to-model authoring capability remain applicable.\\n\\n### REQ-AC-FD-001 — Discover supported tool contracts\\n\\n**Input:** an optional requested operation, exact method/profile and capability\\nquery. **Output/checks:** a versioned inventory of public operations, input/output\\ncontracts, compatible method/profile bindings, supported representations,\\nchecked fragments, effect/access prerequisites, qualification scope and explicit\\nunsupported cases. Unknown or unsupported requests return their exact reason\\nand unmet contract. **Limit:** availability selects no method, frame, role,\\nworkflow or next action; the interface must be usable by all three F_P actors\\nwithout private study knowledge. Protocol, CLI/MCP, schema and provider are HOW.\\nOwners: [PDEF](fd-source-owner-map.md#pdef) §8/11;\\n[RF](fd-source-owner-map.md#rf) RF-016;\\n[ASSURE](fd-source-owner-map.md#assure) §13.\\n\\n### REQ-AC-FD-002 — Bind and observe exact workspace inputs\\n\\n**Input:** caller-selected Product scope/definition, exact operative method and\\noptional profile, declared material observation scope and access grant.\\n**Output/checks:** resolved identities/content digests and observation evidence\\nfor the selected definition, method, subject, configuration/dependencies and\\ncurrent relevant workspace bytes, including dirty/untracked content. Distinguish\\nthe tool's builder basis, consumer operating basis and represented subject cuts;\\nreport ambiguous, inaccessible, changed or unsupported bindings without\\nsubstitution. Reobservation compares the supplied material preconditions before\\na dependent tool effect. **Limit:** branch/HEAD alone is not mutable state;\\nobservation establishes only the acquired scope/time and neither adopts latest\\nnor composes sibling Products/bases. Owners:\\n[PDEF](fd-source-owner-map.md#pdef) §4/12;\\n[RF](fd-source-owner-map.md#rf) RF-005;\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[1,50]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"e3fcebd7e9fbc60dc36ed4c02ee834a96f14226af134809c938169d4712dfc23\",\"selected_sha256\":\"a098570b35bf6eda470a3b2ea3939c7059dd89ee0bf7bcbd7cdad4246f55a597\",\"size_bytes\":2929,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"specification/requirements/fd-support-tools.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1,50]},\"sha256\":\"e3fcebd7e9fbc60dc36ed4c02ee834a96f14226af134809c938169d4712dfc23\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9ee27ae-0996-4105-ba6f-30f3c0f28675","uuid":"72f3df3c-b50d-445e-906e-178804d2f608","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:26:27.935Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:9c6fa357a6785c2d42508d7f6fa47ccfb9b1f753eaedd64e3bc82629ad7e3491\",\"sha256\":\"9c6fa357a6785c2d42508d7f6fa47ccfb9b1f753eaedd64e3bc82629ad7e3491\"},\"id\":\"r-fdt-1\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=8b58fa747b08b4d8d7aa0fc7d8bfb2f4a4e47e6fa84e7ec659f0e37feb798fc9]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"# Deterministic Support Tools for F_P Actors\\n\\n**Family**: REQ-AC-FD-*\\n**Status**: Deferred\\n**Category**: Capability\\n\\nThis family specifies additional tools supporting F_P Executives, Workers and\\nReviewers. Deferred means owning design and realization are pending; the Product\\noutcome is retained. STDO3.0 owns the methodology and its contracts. The\\n[source-owner map](fd-source-owner-map.md) binds the exact provisional derivation\\nreference and the owner clauses cited below. Runtime use consumes the caller's\\nexact selected method/profile through a declared supported binding, without\\nadopting that provisional candidate or changing a_c's installed builder basis.\\n\\nEvery operation has an exact versioned input/output contract and reproducible\\nchecks over its supplied inputs. External observations retain their identity,\\nscope and time. A named source/carrier/dispatch/write operation is distinct from\\nan `F_D[v]` evaluation/proof returning a judgment; neither makes the invoked\\nF_P operation or its semantic answer deterministic. Existing AC-R-001..015 and\\nthe separate F_P source-to-model authoring capability remain applicable.\\n\\n### REQ-AC-FD-001 — Discover supported tool contracts\\n\\n**Input:** an optional requested operation, exact method/profile and capability\\nquery. **Output/checks:** a versioned inventory of public operations, input/output\\ncontracts, compatible method/profile bindings, supported representations,\\nchecked fragments, effect/access prerequisites, qualification scope and explicit\\nunsupported cases. Unknown or unsupported requests return their exact reason\\nand unmet contract. **Limit:** availability selects no method, frame, role,\\nworkflow or next action; the interface must be usable by all three F_P actors\\nwithout private study knowledge. Protocol, CLI/MCP, schema and provider are HOW.\\nOwners: [PDEF](fd-source-owner-map.md#pdef) §8/11;\\n[RF](fd-source-owner-map.md#rf) RF-016;\\n[ASSURE](fd-source-owner-map.md#assure) §13.\\n\\n### REQ-AC-FD-002 — Bind and observe exact workspace inputs\\n\\n**Input:** caller-selected Product scope/definition, exact operative method and\\noptional profile, declared material observation scope and access grant.\\n**Output/checks:** resolved identities/content digests and observation evidence\\nfor the selected definition, method, subject, configuration/dependencies and\\ncurrent relevant workspace bytes, including dirty/untracked content. Distinguish\\nthe tool's builder basis, consumer operating basis and represented subject cuts;\\nreport ambiguous, inaccessible, changed or unsupported bindings without\\nsubstitution. Reobservation compares the supplied material preconditions before\\na dependent tool effect. **Limit:** branch/HEAD alone is not mutable state;\\nobservation establishes only the acquired scope/time and neither adopts latest\\nnor composes sibling Products/bases. Owners:\\n[PDEF](fd-source-owner-map.md#pdef) §4/12;\\n[RF](fd-source-owner-map.md#rf) RF-005;\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[1,50]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"e3fcebd7e9fbc60dc36ed4c02ee834a96f14226af134809c938169d4712dfc23\",\"selected_sha256\":\"a098570b35bf6eda470a3b2ea3939c7059dd89ee0bf7bcbd7cdad4246f55a597\",\"size_bytes\":2929,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"specification/requirements/fd-support-tools.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1,50]},\"sha256\":\"e3fcebd7e9fbc60dc36ed4c02ee834a96f14226af134809c938169d4712dfc23\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:9c6fa357a6785c2d42508d7f6fa47ccfb9b1f753eaedd64e3bc82629ad7e3491","sha256":"9c6fa357a6785c2d42508d7f6fa47ccfb9b1f753eaedd64e3bc82629ad7e3491"},"id":"r-fdt-1","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=8b58fa747b08b4d8d7aa0fc7d8bfb2f4a4e47e6fa84e7ec659f0e37feb798fc9]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"# Deterministic Support Tools for F_P Actors\n\n**Family**: REQ-AC-FD-*\n**Status**: Deferred\n**Category**: Capability\n\nThis family specifies additional tools supporting F_P Executives, Workers and\nReviewers. Deferred means owning design and realization are pending; the Product\noutcome is retained. STDO3.0 owns the methodology and its contracts. The\n[source-owner map](fd-source-owner-map.md) binds the exact provisional derivation\nreference and the owner clauses cited below. Runtime use consumes the caller's\nexact selected method/profile through a declared supported binding, without\nadopting that provisional candidate or changing a_c's installed builder basis.\n\nEvery operation has an exact versioned input/output contract and reproducible\nchecks over its supplied inputs. External observations retain their identity,\nscope and time. A named source/carrier/dispatch/write operation is distinct from\nan `F_D[v]` evaluation/proof returning a judgment; neither makes the invoked\nF_P operation or its semantic answer deterministic. Existing AC-R-001..015 and\nthe separate F_P source-to-model authoring capability remain applicable.\n\n### REQ-AC-FD-001 — Discover supported tool contracts\n\n**Input:** an optional requested operation, exact method/profile and capability\nquery. **Output/checks:** a versioned inventory of public operations, input/output\ncontracts, compatible method/profile bindings, supported representations,\nchecked fragments, effect/access prerequisites, qualification scope and explicit\nunsupported cases. Unknown or unsupported requests return their exact reason\nand unmet contract. **Limit:** availability selects no method, frame, role,\nworkflow or next action; the interface must be usable by all three F_P actors\nwithout private study knowledge. Protocol, CLI/MCP, schema and provider are HOW.\nOwners: [PDEF](fd-source-owner-map.md#pdef) §8/11;\n[RF](fd-source-owner-map.md#rf) RF-016;\n[ASSURE](fd-source-owner-map.md#assure) §13.\n\n### REQ-AC-FD-002 — Bind and observe exact workspace inputs\n\n**Input:** caller-selected Product scope/definition, exact operative method and\noptional profile, declared material observation scope and access grant.\n**Output/checks:** resolved identities/content digests and observation evidence\nfor the selected definition, method, subject, configuration/dependencies and\ncurrent relevant workspace bytes, including dirty/untracked content. Distinguish\nthe tool's builder basis, consumer operating basis and represented subject cuts;\nreport ambiguous, inaccessible, changed or unsupported bindings without\nsubstitution. Reobservation compares the supplied material preconditions before\na dependent tool effect. **Limit:** branch/HEAD alone is not mutable state;\nobservation establishes only the acquired scope/time and neither adopts latest\nnor composes sibling Products/bases. Owners:\n[PDEF](fd-source-owner-map.md#pdef) §4/12;\n[RF](fd-source-owner-map.md#rf) RF-005;\n","coordinates":{"lines":[1,50]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"e3fcebd7e9fbc60dc36ed4c02ee834a96f14226af134809c938169d4712dfc23","selected_sha256":"a098570b35bf6eda470a3b2ea3939c7059dd89ee0bf7bcbd7cdad4246f55a597","size_bytes":2929,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"specification/requirements/fd-support-tools.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[1,50]},"sha256":"e3fcebd7e9fbc60dc36ed4c02ee834a96f14226af134809c938169d4712dfc23"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DWGZeDqC6RvKbsQpvDxLem","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAxkN6EdBxB8ZLA6Vvqh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DFRqTknhTEVyve74Mam6B1","name":"mcp__ac_review__source_read","input":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"r-fdv-1","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"specification/requirements/fd-support-verification.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[1,50]},"sha256":"3746e614a5ddc3f0a551e926998f16d6101cc037c5c43b879b4447b017a8dbdf"},"encoding":"utf8","max_content_bytes":8192}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5306,"cache_read_input_tokens":65689,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5306},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9ee27ae-0996-4105-ba6f-30f3c0f28675","uuid":"4ef032fa-f411-4146-8bc1-aeb2186cb496","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:26:30.262Z","request_id":"req_011CgAxkMk9vu5Gpfmz7tbaH","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01DFRqTknhTEVyve74Mam6B1":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"r-fdv-1","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"specification/requirements/fd-support-verification.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[1,50]},"sha256":"3746e614a5ddc3f0a551e926998f16d6101cc037c5c43b879b4447b017a8dbdf"},"encoding":"utf8","max_content_bytes":8192}}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DFRqTknhTEVyve74Mam6B1","display_name":"Source Read","server_display_name":"a_c.graphify.fd-support","tool_name":"source.read"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DFRqTknhTEVyve74Mam6B1","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:85712a930f86c7f1a55770587ff18395f37d32b54b7b85fc047fb7cf424db43a\",\"sha256\":\"85712a930f86c7f1a55770587ff18395f37d32b54b7b85fc047fb7cf424db43a\"},\"id\":\"r-fdv-1\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=275b67136d4f6eaeb1d88962c8c1f9dd37077ca8ffa836db1159a41488f60c90]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"# Deterministic Support Tool Qualification\\n\\n**Family**: REQ-AC-FDV-*\\n**Status**: Deferred\\n**Category**: Verification\\n\\nThis family qualifies the [additional tools](fd-support-tools.md), not the\\nSTDO3.0 methodology or F_P actor judgments. Design, implementation and executed\\nqualification remain pending. Owners are the exact provisional clauses in the\\n[source-owner map](fd-source-owner-map.md), consumed through the caller-selected\\noperative method rather than adopted as a new a_c builder basis.\\n\\n### REQ-AC-FDV-001 — Qualify observable tool contracts on a real use path\\n\\nFor each claimed operation, bind exact inputs, deterministic output/check\\npredicate, scope, expected counterexample and method-owner contract. Verify\\nreproducibility over frozen inputs and preserve the scope/time of external\\nobservations. Exercise the documented ordinary interfaces with F_P Executive,\\nWorker and Reviewer callers on one real bounded development task, including\\nactual context/source acquisition, executor boundary, proof/review evidence\\nand durable return/recording routes selected for that task. Distinguish\\ncontract sufficiency, actual boundary exchanges, runnable path and actor\\nusability; do not substitute private study success or fixture knowledge. F_P\\nassessment, required independence and owner disposition are provided by their\\nexisting owners, not by the tools. Each unexercised operation/variant remains\\nan explicit qualification gap. Owners: [EVAL](fd-source-owner-map.md#eval)\\n§1/3/6; [ASSURE](fd-source-owner-map.md#assure) §3/13–16.\\n\\n### REQ-AC-FDV-002 — Qualify refusal, unknown and recovery discriminators\\n\\nExecute positive and relevant negative/control cases for the inventory below,\\nwith exact tool/method/profile/candidate identities, assertion and execution\\nprovenance, actual supplied context/settings, raw attempts, expected observable\\nchecks/refusals and retained unknowns. Different source conditions must yield\\nthe owner-contract distinctions; an always-refuse or always-pass implementation\\ncannot qualify them. Demonstrate handoff/resumption from named durable sources\\nwithout hidden actor context. These scenarios test the tool response to supplied\\nrules and observations, not an a_c-owned workflow or semantic truth oracle.\\nAn independent tenant can apply the same carrier-neutral contract without\\nGraphify, a V3 runtime dependency or study-private machinery. Owners:\\n[ACT](fd-source-owner-map.md#act) §1 Applicability/2/3/5/7;\\n[FOUND](fd-source-owner-map.md#found) Results/Conjunction of results;\\n[ASSURE](fd-source-owner-map.md#assure) §3/13.\\n\\n### REQ-AC-FDV-003 — Evaluate accepted-result benefit separately\\n\\nBefore claiming improved discovery, quality, consistency or efficiency, compare\\nmatched real tasks with/without the declared tool support under exact\\nsource/method, actor/envelope/settings and outcome/acceptance criteria. Retain\\nsemantic/coverage/acceptance evidence and all material acquisition, F_P authoring,\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[1,50]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"3746e614a5ddc3f0a551e926998f16d6101cc037c5c43b879b4447b017a8dbdf\",\"selected_sha256\":\"de284147e03decaad016c939e7dae5d1efaaf957d63b21e56dd6908b4036f493\",\"size_bytes\":2956,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"specification/requirements/fd-support-verification.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1,50]},\"sha256\":\"3746e614a5ddc3f0a551e926998f16d6101cc037c5c43b879b4447b017a8dbdf\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9ee27ae-0996-4105-ba6f-30f3c0f28675","uuid":"1652da64-7a27-4b57-9b82-7bd903e6efd2","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:26:30.446Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:85712a930f86c7f1a55770587ff18395f37d32b54b7b85fc047fb7cf424db43a\",\"sha256\":\"85712a930f86c7f1a55770587ff18395f37d32b54b7b85fc047fb7cf424db43a\"},\"id\":\"r-fdv-1\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=275b67136d4f6eaeb1d88962c8c1f9dd37077ca8ffa836db1159a41488f60c90]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"# Deterministic Support Tool Qualification\\n\\n**Family**: REQ-AC-FDV-*\\n**Status**: Deferred\\n**Category**: Verification\\n\\nThis family qualifies the [additional tools](fd-support-tools.md), not the\\nSTDO3.0 methodology or F_P actor judgments. Design, implementation and executed\\nqualification remain pending. Owners are the exact provisional clauses in the\\n[source-owner map](fd-source-owner-map.md), consumed through the caller-selected\\noperative method rather than adopted as a new a_c builder basis.\\n\\n### REQ-AC-FDV-001 — Qualify observable tool contracts on a real use path\\n\\nFor each claimed operation, bind exact inputs, deterministic output/check\\npredicate, scope, expected counterexample and method-owner contract. Verify\\nreproducibility over frozen inputs and preserve the scope/time of external\\nobservations. Exercise the documented ordinary interfaces with F_P Executive,\\nWorker and Reviewer callers on one real bounded development task, including\\nactual context/source acquisition, executor boundary, proof/review evidence\\nand durable return/recording routes selected for that task. Distinguish\\ncontract sufficiency, actual boundary exchanges, runnable path and actor\\nusability; do not substitute private study success or fixture knowledge. F_P\\nassessment, required independence and owner disposition are provided by their\\nexisting owners, not by the tools. Each unexercised operation/variant remains\\nan explicit qualification gap. Owners: [EVAL](fd-source-owner-map.md#eval)\\n§1/3/6; [ASSURE](fd-source-owner-map.md#assure) §3/13–16.\\n\\n### REQ-AC-FDV-002 — Qualify refusal, unknown and recovery discriminators\\n\\nExecute positive and relevant negative/control cases for the inventory below,\\nwith exact tool/method/profile/candidate identities, assertion and execution\\nprovenance, actual supplied context/settings, raw attempts, expected observable\\nchecks/refusals and retained unknowns. Different source conditions must yield\\nthe owner-contract distinctions; an always-refuse or always-pass implementation\\ncannot qualify them. Demonstrate handoff/resumption from named durable sources\\nwithout hidden actor context. These scenarios test the tool response to supplied\\nrules and observations, not an a_c-owned workflow or semantic truth oracle.\\nAn independent tenant can apply the same carrier-neutral contract without\\nGraphify, a V3 runtime dependency or study-private machinery. Owners:\\n[ACT](fd-source-owner-map.md#act) §1 Applicability/2/3/5/7;\\n[FOUND](fd-source-owner-map.md#found) Results/Conjunction of results;\\n[ASSURE](fd-source-owner-map.md#assure) §3/13.\\n\\n### REQ-AC-FDV-003 — Evaluate accepted-result benefit separately\\n\\nBefore claiming improved discovery, quality, consistency or efficiency, compare\\nmatched real tasks with/without the declared tool support under exact\\nsource/method, actor/envelope/settings and outcome/acceptance criteria. Retain\\nsemantic/coverage/acceptance evidence and all material acquisition, F_P authoring,\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[1,50]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"3746e614a5ddc3f0a551e926998f16d6101cc037c5c43b879b4447b017a8dbdf\",\"selected_sha256\":\"de284147e03decaad016c939e7dae5d1efaaf957d63b21e56dd6908b4036f493\",\"size_bytes\":2956,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"specification/requirements/fd-support-verification.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1,50]},\"sha256\":\"3746e614a5ddc3f0a551e926998f16d6101cc037c5c43b879b4447b017a8dbdf\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:85712a930f86c7f1a55770587ff18395f37d32b54b7b85fc047fb7cf424db43a","sha256":"85712a930f86c7f1a55770587ff18395f37d32b54b7b85fc047fb7cf424db43a"},"id":"r-fdv-1","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=275b67136d4f6eaeb1d88962c8c1f9dd37077ca8ffa836db1159a41488f60c90]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"# Deterministic Support Tool Qualification\n\n**Family**: REQ-AC-FDV-*\n**Status**: Deferred\n**Category**: Verification\n\nThis family qualifies the [additional tools](fd-support-tools.md), not the\nSTDO3.0 methodology or F_P actor judgments. Design, implementation and executed\nqualification remain pending. Owners are the exact provisional clauses in the\n[source-owner map](fd-source-owner-map.md), consumed through the caller-selected\noperative method rather than adopted as a new a_c builder basis.\n\n### REQ-AC-FDV-001 — Qualify observable tool contracts on a real use path\n\nFor each claimed operation, bind exact inputs, deterministic output/check\npredicate, scope, expected counterexample and method-owner contract. Verify\nreproducibility over frozen inputs and preserve the scope/time of external\nobservations. Exercise the documented ordinary interfaces with F_P Executive,\nWorker and Reviewer callers on one real bounded development task, including\nactual context/source acquisition, executor boundary, proof/review evidence\nand durable return/recording routes selected for that task. Distinguish\ncontract sufficiency, actual boundary exchanges, runnable path and actor\nusability; do not substitute private study success or fixture knowledge. F_P\nassessment, required independence and owner disposition are provided by their\nexisting owners, not by the tools. Each unexercised operation/variant remains\nan explicit qualification gap. Owners: [EVAL](fd-source-owner-map.md#eval)\n§1/3/6; [ASSURE](fd-source-owner-map.md#assure) §3/13–16.\n\n### REQ-AC-FDV-002 — Qualify refusal, unknown and recovery discriminators\n\nExecute positive and relevant negative/control cases for the inventory below,\nwith exact tool/method/profile/candidate identities, assertion and execution\nprovenance, actual supplied context/settings, raw attempts, expected observable\nchecks/refusals and retained unknowns. Different source conditions must yield\nthe owner-contract distinctions; an always-refuse or always-pass implementation\ncannot qualify them. Demonstrate handoff/resumption from named durable sources\nwithout hidden actor context. These scenarios test the tool response to supplied\nrules and observations, not an a_c-owned workflow or semantic truth oracle.\nAn independent tenant can apply the same carrier-neutral contract without\nGraphify, a V3 runtime dependency or study-private machinery. Owners:\n[ACT](fd-source-owner-map.md#act) §1 Applicability/2/3/5/7;\n[FOUND](fd-source-owner-map.md#found) Results/Conjunction of results;\n[ASSURE](fd-source-owner-map.md#assure) §3/13.\n\n### REQ-AC-FDV-003 — Evaluate accepted-result benefit separately\n\nBefore claiming improved discovery, quality, consistency or efficiency, compare\nmatched real tasks with/without the declared tool support under exact\nsource/method, actor/envelope/settings and outcome/acceptance criteria. Retain\nsemantic/coverage/acceptance evidence and all material acquisition, F_P authoring,\n","coordinates":{"lines":[1,50]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"3746e614a5ddc3f0a551e926998f16d6101cc037c5c43b879b4447b017a8dbdf","selected_sha256":"de284147e03decaad016c939e7dae5d1efaaf957d63b21e56dd6908b4036f493","size_bytes":2956,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"specification/requirements/fd-support-verification.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[1,50]},"sha256":"3746e614a5ddc3f0a551e926998f16d6101cc037c5c43b879b4447b017a8dbdf"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DFRqTknhTEVyve74Mam6B1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
