{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAxmM9TybtgNA58ZRsAh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016j1cd1fwopGGmzerDKSva2","name":"mcp__ac_review__source_read","input":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"r-asr-1","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"ASSURANCE.md","root":"method","selector":{"lines":[680,756]},"sha256":"e33a6e39e1e93d38dbd3ea212d8d9f0d2f44a366a9345fda762d2481c254d0bf"},"encoding":"utf8","max_content_bytes":8192}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6740,"cache_read_input_tokens":70995,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6740},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9ee27ae-0996-4105-ba6f-30f3c0f28675","uuid":"a88d85bf-1a50-4af3-99a5-086c9263e2ee","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:26:48.525Z","request_id":"req_011CgAxmLpccRwwBKgbNGDaW","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_016j1cd1fwopGGmzerDKSva2":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"r-asr-1","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"ASSURANCE.md","root":"method","selector":{"lines":[680,756]},"sha256":"e33a6e39e1e93d38dbd3ea212d8d9f0d2f44a366a9345fda762d2481c254d0bf"},"encoding":"utf8","max_content_bytes":8192}}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016j1cd1fwopGGmzerDKSva2","display_name":"Source Read","server_display_name":"a_c.graphify.fd-support","tool_name":"source.read"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016j1cd1fwopGGmzerDKSva2","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:433644a2338fa69c69deaf06e78f2a49d20dd3c99b4312da631be43fc524ca37\",\"sha256\":\"433644a2338fa69c69deaf06e78f2a49d20dd3c99b4312da631be43fc524ca37\"},\"id\":\"r-asr-1\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=7932989a461555c8d8f8d758c2b28558da1f722c26dd9bacad582713c0331472]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"## 11. Assurance subject acquisition and evaluation\\n\\nAcquiring the assurance subject and evaluating it are distinct relations\\n(P6, P1; provenance #assurance-subject-acquisition-and-evaluation). Where a\\nclaim depends on owner-issued Product, runtime, lifecycle, admission,\\nreplay or projection truth, the testing frame acquires that truth through\\nthe exact runnable owner surface, validator, projection, receipt or\\nreconstruction relation. A harness, fixture, expected-value builder, proof\\nscript, assurance evaluator or assessor does not reconstruct a parallel\\nowner state from raw payloads, events, logs, filenames, labels or\\nimplementation fragments and then evaluate that self-authored state as if\\nit were the Product subject. Where the acquired observation cannot\\nseparate two admissible subjects on which the assessed predicate takes\\nopposite truth values, the frame returns further evidence, a justified\\nnarrower scope or `indeterminate`. The binding of the\\nobservation itself needs support\\n([FOUNDATIONS §4 Assertions and observation](FOUNDATIONS.md#assertions-and-observation),\\nObservation sufficiency) (P1, P6).\\n\\nAfter lawful acquisition, an independently derived oracle may evaluate the\\ngoverning claim. Generic assurance mechanics may compute bytes, digests,\\nordering, equality, set membership, completeness and conjunction over\\nowner-issued evidence. Those mechanics stay evidence evaluators: they\\ncannot mint owner carriers, choose the current history, select the\\nauthoritative path, interpret domain lifecycle or admission meaning, or\\nbecome a runtime fallback (P6; EVALUATION §2).\\n\\nThe rule does not require an evaluator to trust the implementation under\\ntest as its semantic oracle; the oracle derives from Product, requirement\\nand accepted-design law. It requires the assurance subject to be the actual\\nowner-issued subject rather than a second implementation of the owner's\\nruntime meaning. If the required owner projection or observable seam is\\nabsent, the result keeps a named assurance or design gap; the proof harness\\ndoes not fill it with rival semantics (P6, P5).\\n\\n## 12. Counterexample localisation\\n\\nA testing counterexample is returned to its earliest supported causal\\nfrontier on the declared path. The frontier holds the causally minimal\\nviolated owner relations or seam coordinates the evidence establishes;\\nearliest means minimal under the declared causal relation, not first in log\\nor clock order (P5, P6; provenance #counterexample-localization).\\n\\nThe localisation result represents exactly one of (P5, P1):\\n\\n- one unique violated locus;\\n- a jointly established set of incomparable earliest violated loci whose\\n  combined violation is necessary to the supported causal explanation;\\n- unresolved alternative frontiers, when the evidence supports several\\n  possible causal explanations but cannot establish which occurred; or\\n- `indeterminate`, when the evidence cannot support a bounded frontier.\\n\\nThe four forms are a refinement of the core under the rule of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results), for the predicate \\\"the\\nevidence establishes the counterexample's earliest violated loci on the\\ndeclared path\\\". One unique violated locus and a jointly established set\\nmap to `satisfied`. Unresolved alternative frontiers map to\\n`indeterminate`, naming the alternatives that further evidence must\\ndecide between. The fourth form is the core value `indeterminate` itself,\\nnaming the evidence a bounded frontier needs. The form travels with the\\nvalue as the domain outcome, so a joint set stays distinct from a unique\\nlocus and unresolved alternatives stay distinct from an unbounded\\nfrontier. Purpose and material relation: a localisation combines with\\nother results in the one core, and an unresolved causal explanation is\\nnever read as an established one (P5, P1, P6).\\n\\nLocalisation records the subject, basis, frontier form and members, causal\\nevidence, expected relations, the observed counterexample and the\\ndownstream claims it invalidates. It does not collapse a jointly\\nestablished set into one arbitrary owner, and it does not report\\nunresolved alternatives as a joint cause (P5, P4b).\\n\\nA localised frontier does not itself authorise broader test expansion,\\ncompatibility repair, another controller or a reinterpretation of unchanged\\nupstream meaning. A resulting scope or design change follows the existing\\nre-entry relation (SPEC_METHOD §4; P6).\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[680,756]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"e33a6e39e1e93d38dbd3ea212d8d9f0d2f44a366a9345fda762d2481c254d0bf\",\"selected_sha256\":\"25be90aa160d0bef429091772d88e3f099c9acee5cf177c9356af01758b1aa6d\",\"size_bytes\":4400,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"ASSURANCE.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[680,756]},\"sha256\":\"e33a6e39e1e93d38dbd3ea212d8d9f0d2f44a366a9345fda762d2481c254d0bf\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9ee27ae-0996-4105-ba6f-30f3c0f28675","uuid":"220fdd63-c0fb-47f8-8f24-eec81c73c9a6","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:26:48.537Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:433644a2338fa69c69deaf06e78f2a49d20dd3c99b4312da631be43fc524ca37\",\"sha256\":\"433644a2338fa69c69deaf06e78f2a49d20dd3c99b4312da631be43fc524ca37\"},\"id\":\"r-asr-1\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=7932989a461555c8d8f8d758c2b28558da1f722c26dd9bacad582713c0331472]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"## 11. Assurance subject acquisition and evaluation\\n\\nAcquiring the assurance subject and evaluating it are distinct relations\\n(P6, P1; provenance #assurance-subject-acquisition-and-evaluation). Where a\\nclaim depends on owner-issued Product, runtime, lifecycle, admission,\\nreplay or projection truth, the testing frame acquires that truth through\\nthe exact runnable owner surface, validator, projection, receipt or\\nreconstruction relation. A harness, fixture, expected-value builder, proof\\nscript, assurance evaluator or assessor does not reconstruct a parallel\\nowner state from raw payloads, events, logs, filenames, labels or\\nimplementation fragments and then evaluate that self-authored state as if\\nit were the Product subject. Where the acquired observation cannot\\nseparate two admissible subjects on which the assessed predicate takes\\nopposite truth values, the frame returns further evidence, a justified\\nnarrower scope or `indeterminate`. The binding of the\\nobservation itself needs support\\n([FOUNDATIONS §4 Assertions and observation](FOUNDATIONS.md#assertions-and-observation),\\nObservation sufficiency) (P1, P6).\\n\\nAfter lawful acquisition, an independently derived oracle may evaluate the\\ngoverning claim. Generic assurance mechanics may compute bytes, digests,\\nordering, equality, set membership, completeness and conjunction over\\nowner-issued evidence. Those mechanics stay evidence evaluators: they\\ncannot mint owner carriers, choose the current history, select the\\nauthoritative path, interpret domain lifecycle or admission meaning, or\\nbecome a runtime fallback (P6; EVALUATION §2).\\n\\nThe rule does not require an evaluator to trust the implementation under\\ntest as its semantic oracle; the oracle derives from Product, requirement\\nand accepted-design law. It requires the assurance subject to be the actual\\nowner-issued subject rather than a second implementation of the owner's\\nruntime meaning. If the required owner projection or observable seam is\\nabsent, the result keeps a named assurance or design gap; the proof harness\\ndoes not fill it with rival semantics (P6, P5).\\n\\n## 12. Counterexample localisation\\n\\nA testing counterexample is returned to its earliest supported causal\\nfrontier on the declared path. The frontier holds the causally minimal\\nviolated owner relations or seam coordinates the evidence establishes;\\nearliest means minimal under the declared causal relation, not first in log\\nor clock order (P5, P6; provenance #counterexample-localization).\\n\\nThe localisation result represents exactly one of (P5, P1):\\n\\n- one unique violated locus;\\n- a jointly established set of incomparable earliest violated loci whose\\n  combined violation is necessary to the supported causal explanation;\\n- unresolved alternative frontiers, when the evidence supports several\\n  possible causal explanations but cannot establish which occurred; or\\n- `indeterminate`, when the evidence cannot support a bounded frontier.\\n\\nThe four forms are a refinement of the core under the rule of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results), for the predicate \\\"the\\nevidence establishes the counterexample's earliest violated loci on the\\ndeclared path\\\". One unique violated locus and a jointly established set\\nmap to `satisfied`. Unresolved alternative frontiers map to\\n`indeterminate`, naming the alternatives that further evidence must\\ndecide between. The fourth form is the core value `indeterminate` itself,\\nnaming the evidence a bounded frontier needs. The form travels with the\\nvalue as the domain outcome, so a joint set stays distinct from a unique\\nlocus and unresolved alternatives stay distinct from an unbounded\\nfrontier. Purpose and material relation: a localisation combines with\\nother results in the one core, and an unresolved causal explanation is\\nnever read as an established one (P5, P1, P6).\\n\\nLocalisation records the subject, basis, frontier form and members, causal\\nevidence, expected relations, the observed counterexample and the\\ndownstream claims it invalidates. It does not collapse a jointly\\nestablished set into one arbitrary owner, and it does not report\\nunresolved alternatives as a joint cause (P5, P4b).\\n\\nA localised frontier does not itself authorise broader test expansion,\\ncompatibility repair, another controller or a reinterpretation of unchanged\\nupstream meaning. A resulting scope or design change follows the existing\\nre-entry relation (SPEC_METHOD §4; P6).\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[680,756]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"e33a6e39e1e93d38dbd3ea212d8d9f0d2f44a366a9345fda762d2481c254d0bf\",\"selected_sha256\":\"25be90aa160d0bef429091772d88e3f099c9acee5cf177c9356af01758b1aa6d\",\"size_bytes\":4400,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"ASSURANCE.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[680,756]},\"sha256\":\"e33a6e39e1e93d38dbd3ea212d8d9f0d2f44a366a9345fda762d2481c254d0bf\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:433644a2338fa69c69deaf06e78f2a49d20dd3c99b4312da631be43fc524ca37","sha256":"433644a2338fa69c69deaf06e78f2a49d20dd3c99b4312da631be43fc524ca37"},"id":"r-asr-1","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=7932989a461555c8d8f8d758c2b28558da1f722c26dd9bacad582713c0331472]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"## 11. Assurance subject acquisition and evaluation\n\nAcquiring the assurance subject and evaluating it are distinct relations\n(P6, P1; provenance #assurance-subject-acquisition-and-evaluation). Where a\nclaim depends on owner-issued Product, runtime, lifecycle, admission,\nreplay or projection truth, the testing frame acquires that truth through\nthe exact runnable owner surface, validator, projection, receipt or\nreconstruction relation. A harness, fixture, expected-value builder, proof\nscript, assurance evaluator or assessor does not reconstruct a parallel\nowner state from raw payloads, events, logs, filenames, labels or\nimplementation fragments and then evaluate that self-authored state as if\nit were the Product subject. Where the acquired observation cannot\nseparate two admissible subjects on which the assessed predicate takes\nopposite truth values, the frame returns further evidence, a justified\nnarrower scope or `indeterminate`. The binding of the\nobservation itself needs support\n([FOUNDATIONS §4 Assertions and observation](FOUNDATIONS.md#assertions-and-observation),\nObservation sufficiency) (P1, P6).\n\nAfter lawful acquisition, an independently derived oracle may evaluate the\ngoverning claim. Generic assurance mechanics may compute bytes, digests,\nordering, equality, set membership, completeness and conjunction over\nowner-issued evidence. Those mechanics stay evidence evaluators: they\ncannot mint owner carriers, choose the current history, select the\nauthoritative path, interpret domain lifecycle or admission meaning, or\nbecome a runtime fallback (P6; EVALUATION §2).\n\nThe rule does not require an evaluator to trust the implementation under\ntest as its semantic oracle; the oracle derives from Product, requirement\nand accepted-design law. It requires the assurance subject to be the actual\nowner-issued subject rather than a second implementation of the owner's\nruntime meaning. If the required owner projection or observable seam is\nabsent, the result keeps a named assurance or design gap; the proof harness\ndoes not fill it with rival semantics (P6, P5).\n\n## 12. Counterexample localisation\n\nA testing counterexample is returned to its earliest supported causal\nfrontier on the declared path. The frontier holds the causally minimal\nviolated owner relations or seam coordinates the evidence establishes;\nearliest means minimal under the declared causal relation, not first in log\nor clock order (P5, P6; provenance #counterexample-localization).\n\nThe localisation result represents exactly one of (P5, P1):\n\n- one unique violated locus;\n- a jointly established set of incomparable earliest violated loci whose\n  combined violation is necessary to the supported causal explanation;\n- unresolved alternative frontiers, when the evidence supports several\n  possible causal explanations but cannot establish which occurred; or\n- `indeterminate`, when the evidence cannot support a bounded frontier.\n\nThe four forms are a refinement of the core under the rule of\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results), for the predicate \"the\nevidence establishes the counterexample's earliest violated loci on the\ndeclared path\". One unique violated locus and a jointly established set\nmap to `satisfied`. Unresolved alternative frontiers map to\n`indeterminate`, naming the alternatives that further evidence must\ndecide between. The fourth form is the core value `indeterminate` itself,\nnaming the evidence a bounded frontier needs. The form travels with the\nvalue as the domain outcome, so a joint set stays distinct from a unique\nlocus and unresolved alternatives stay distinct from an unbounded\nfrontier. Purpose and material relation: a localisation combines with\nother results in the one core, and an unresolved causal explanation is\nnever read as an established one (P5, P1, P6).\n\nLocalisation records the subject, basis, frontier form and members, causal\nevidence, expected relations, the observed counterexample and the\ndownstream claims it invalidates. It does not collapse a jointly\nestablished set into one arbitrary owner, and it does not report\nunresolved alternatives as a joint cause (P5, P4b).\n\nA localised frontier does not itself authorise broader test expansion,\ncompatibility repair, another controller or a reinterpretation of unchanged\nupstream meaning. A resulting scope or design change follows the existing\nre-entry relation (SPEC_METHOD §4; P6).\n\n","coordinates":{"lines":[680,756]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"e33a6e39e1e93d38dbd3ea212d8d9f0d2f44a366a9345fda762d2481c254d0bf","selected_sha256":"25be90aa160d0bef429091772d88e3f099c9acee5cf177c9356af01758b1aa6d","size_bytes":4400,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"ASSURANCE.md","root":"method","selector":{"lines":[680,756]},"sha256":"e33a6e39e1e93d38dbd3ea212d8d9f0d2f44a366a9345fda762d2481c254d0bf"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016j1cd1fwopGGmzerDKSva2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
