e exact applicable upstream contract; the table does not redefine its states,\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[51,64]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"3746e614a5ddc3f0a551e926998f16d6101cc037c5c43b879b4447b017a8dbdf\",\"selected_sha256\":\"7275a08e17fa5ac9a6a28b085527b4dabd78dd9c731a6b8fc0ed319c3c579887\",\"size_bytes\":743,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"specification/requirements/fd-support-verification.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[51,64]},\"sha256\":\"3746e614a5ddc3f0a551e926998f16d6101cc037c5c43b879b4447b017a8dbdf\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:53f040eae9d69ce0bf0175fba09e05ce8975429fe02dd22edc9f469a8398f210","sha256":"53f040eae9d69ce0bf0175fba09e05ce8975429fe02dd22edc9f469a8398f210"},"id":"r-fdv-3","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=07be11ca68e792a4effd26127b0a541854c00719c3a2caecdf02c433a7d57c24]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"context preparation, refresh, invocation, failed attempts/retries, repair,\nreview and decision effort, with measurement boundaries and unknowns. Report\nobserved differences and limitations rather than inferring a general benefit\nfrom count, graph size, fit or structural success. Owners:\n[ACT](fd-source-owner-map.md#act) §6;\n[EVAL](fd-source-owner-map.md#eval) §1;\n[FOUND](fd-source-owner-map.md#found) Assertions and observation/Change impact\nand evidence reuse.\n\n## Scenario and requirement trace\n\nThe following is written test-case authority, not executed evidence. FD-nnn\nexpands to `REQ-AC-FD-nnn`; FDV-nnn expands to `REQ-AC-FDV-nnn`. Each case supplies\nthe exact applicable upstream contract; the table does not redefine its states,\n","coordinates":{"lines":[51,64]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"3746e614a5ddc3f0a551e926998f16d6101cc037c5c43b879b4447b017a8dbdf","selected_sha256":"7275a08e17fa5ac9a6a28b085527b4dabd78dd9c731a6b8fc0ed319c3c579887","size_bytes":743,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"specification/requirements/fd-support-verification.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[51,64]},"sha256":"3746e614a5ddc3f0a551e926998f16d6101cc037c5c43b879b4447b017a8dbdf"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FDYFLH36wMnR8eohpy2S1R","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAxngYKJsSaBF8FW4e54","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Y2AgUt6ECjRbzNoNDnyhBV","name":"mcp__ac_review__source_read","input":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"r-fdt-3","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"specification/requirements/fd-support-tools.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[111,170]},"sha256":"e3fcebd7e9fbc60dc36ed4c02ee834a96f14226af134809c938169d4712dfc23"},"encoding":"utf8","max_content_bytes":8192}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5855,"cache_read_input_tokens":77735,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5855},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9ee27ae-0996-4105-ba6f-30f3c0f28675","uuid":"dd9d0256-1ee4-40f2-87e8-c51f268dd80d","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:27:01.836Z","request_id":"req_011CgAxngHw26U8BQDeU2ffc","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Y2AgUt6ECjRbzNoNDnyhBV":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"r-fdt-3","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"specification/requirements/fd-support-tools.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[111,170]},"sha256":"e3fcebd7e9fbc60dc36ed4c02ee834a96f14226af134809c938169d4712dfc23"},"encoding":"utf8","max_content_bytes":8192}}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Y2AgUt6ECjRbzNoNDnyhBV","display_name":"Source Read","server_display_name":"a_c.graphify.fd-support","tool_name":"source.read"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y2AgUt6ECjRbzNoNDnyhBV","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:0a2e1c4b9b3baab54d1aade101c7344b04bf2f57d2a09fbb87da22f40925e25e\",\"sha256\":\"0a2e1c4b9b3baab54d1aade101c7344b04bf2f57d2a09fbb87da22f40925e25e\"},\"id\":\"r-fdt-3\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=e05892e276837dc36c8793f7d862e627e53be8c9e38deabf8b2902207ec07546]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"invoked, bound to exact contract identity and decision authority. Report missing\\nor mismatched required support before dispatch; retain draft and admitted\\ncoordinates separately under the method's own contract. **Limit:** a successful\\nshape/context check, role name, ticket state or tool invocation cannot mint\\nadmission or work authority. The tool neither drafts a new grant nor admits the\\nupstream outcome. Owners: [ACT](fd-source-owner-map.md#act) §1 Admission;\\n[TICK](fd-source-owner-map.md#tick) §5.\\n\\n### REQ-AC-FD-007 — Dispatch, notify and observe under a supplied grant\\n\\n**Input:** exact preflighted activation/admission, selected executor operation,\\nexisting grant, permitted tools/territory, material preconditions, effective\\ncontext/settings and selected attempt/resource/observation conditions.\\n**Output/checks:** invocation identity, actual supplied payload/settings,\\nacknowledgments, output/partial-output and effect/termination observations with\\nscope/time, retained attempts and decision-relevant return/exception/basis-change\\nnotifications. Check material bindings before the named effect and expose\\nchanged preconditions without silent rebase. **Limit:** the deterministic\\nwrapper does not make F_P output deterministic or semantic evidence of success.\\nRequests, delivery, evaluation, intended effects and their observed end remain\\nseparate under the selected method; timeout/cancel/interruption preserve its\\nunknown-effect semantics. Fallback observation is bounded by supplied conditions,\\nnot a mandatory polling controller. Owners: [ACT](fd-source-owner-map.md#act)\\n§1/3 Effects/5; [EXEC](fd-source-owner-map.md#exec) §6 if selected.\\n\\n### REQ-AC-FD-008 — Capture and check a closed return\\n\\n**Input:** returned payload/transport evidence, original activation and return\\ncontract, expected consumer, exact subject/basis and supplied currentness,\\ndependency and independence predicates/evidence. **Output/checks:** preserved raw\\nreturn and provenance, deterministic binding/format/currentness findings and\\nthe exact declared evaluations, predicates, domain outcomes and residuals that\\nwere actually returned. Identify stale/wrong-subject/wrong-basis, missing,\\nduplicate and conflicting evidence without dropping it; expose non-consumable\\nsupport/gaps to the declared consumer. **Limit:** do not relabel a historical\\nverdict as a new verdict, manufacture a result for an unperformed evaluation or\\ntreat schema validity as semantic assessment/acceptance. A transport failure is\\nreported separately using the selected method contract. Owners:\\n[FOUND](fd-source-owner-map.md#found) Results/Conjunction of results;\\n[RF](fd-source-owner-map.md#rf) RF-012;\\n[ACT](fd-source-owner-map.md#act) §3/7;\\n[EVAL](fd-source-owner-map.md#eval) §4.\\n\\n### REQ-AC-FD-009 — Prepare independently acquirable review evidence\\n\\n**Input:** exact review claim/candidate and composition boundary, caller-selected\\nsource, comparison subjects, proof/evidence population and method-owned\\nindependence/exposure contract. **Output/checks:** independently resolvable raw\\nauthority/candidate/proof acquisition routes, acquired content where requested,\\nexact byte/record comparisons, and separate assertion/expected-result versus\\nexecution provenance. Support expectation recording before candidate exposure\\nand preserve the actual acquisition/exposure record under the supplied contract.\\nWorkers can acquire their implementation/proof context; Reviewers can inspect\\nthe actual candidate, tests/fixtures and source without author-only privileges.\\n**Limit:** diffs and trace/binding checks are not semantic findings, an independent\\nverdict or adoption of a review recommendation as disposition. Owners:\\n[EVAL](fd-source-owner-map.md#eval) §1–4/6;\\n[ASSURE](fd-source-owner-map.md#assure) §3/10/13–16;\\n[EXEC](fd-source-owner-map.md#exec) §9/10/17/19 if selected.\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[111,170]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"e3fcebd7e9fbc60dc36ed4c02ee834a96f14226af134809c938169d4712dfc23\",\"selected_sha256\":\"4cd8a5ffa6c769b503b8f017bfe15a0293278d0afce3406925a40e0433c3dd3e\",\"size_bytes\":3860,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"specification/requirements/fd-support-tools.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[111,170]},\"sha256\":\"e3fcebd7e9fbc60dc36ed4c02ee834a96f14226af134809c938169d4712dfc23\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9ee27ae-0996-4105-ba6f-30f3c0f28675","uuid":"05d924b1-6510-486f-bb1a-2a088097b90e","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:27:01.849Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:0a2e1c4b9b3baab54d1aade101c7344b04bf2f57d2a09fbb87da22f40925e25e\",\"sha256\":\"0a2e1c4b9b3baab54d1aade101c7344b04bf2f57d2a09fbb87da22f40925e25e\"},\"id\":\"r-fdt-3\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=e05892e276837dc36c8793f7d862e627e53be8c9e38deabf8b2902207ec07546]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"invoked, bound to exact contract identity and decision authority. Report missing\\nor mismatched required support before dispatch; retain draft and admitted\\ncoordinates separately under the method's own contract. **Limit:** a successful\\nshape/context check, role name, ticket state or tool invocation cannot mint\\nadmission or work authority. The tool neither drafts a new grant nor admits the\\nupstream outcome. Owners: [ACT](fd-source-owner-map.md#act) §1 Admission;\\n[TICK](fd-source-owner-map.md#tick) §5.\\n\\n### REQ-AC-FD-007 — Dispatch, notify and observe under a supplied grant\\n\\n**Input:** exact preflighted activation/admission, selected executor operation,\\nexisting grant, permitted tools/territory, material preconditions, effective\\ncontext/settings and selected attempt/resource/observation conditions.\\n**Output/checks:** invocation identity, actual supplied payload/settings,\\nacknowledgments, output/partial-output and effect/termination observations with\\nscope/time, retained attempts and decision-relevant return/exception/basis-change\\nnotifications. Check material bindings before the named effect and expose\\nchanged preconditions without silent rebase. **Limit:** the deterministic\\nwrapper does not make F_P output deterministic or semantic evidence of success.\\nRequests, delivery, evaluation, intended effects and their observed end remain\\nseparate under the selected method; timeout/cancel/interruption preserve its\\nunknown-effect semantics. Fallback observation is bounded by supplied conditions,\\nnot a mandatory polling controller. Owners: [ACT](fd-source-owner-map.md#act)\\n§1/3 Effects/5; [EXEC](fd-source-owner-map.md#exec) §6 if selected.\\n\\n### REQ-AC-FD-008 — Capture and check a closed return\\n\\n**Input:** returned payload/transport evidence, original activation and return\\ncontract, expected consumer, exact subject/basis and supplied currentness,\\ndependency and independence predicates/evidence. **Output/checks:** preserved raw\\nreturn and provenance, deterministic binding/format/currentness findings and\\nthe exact declared evaluations, predicates, domain outcomes and residuals that\\nwere actually returned. Identify stale/wrong-subject/wrong-basis, missing,\\nduplicate and conflicting evidence without dropping it; expose non-consumable\\nsupport/gaps to the declared consumer. **Limit:** do not relabel a historical\\nverdict as a new verdict, manufacture a result for an unperformed evaluation or\\ntreat schema validity as semantic assessment/acceptance. A transport failure is\\nreported separately using the selected method contract. Owners:\\n[FOUND](fd-source-owner-map.md#found) Results/Conjunction of results;\\n[RF](fd-source-owner-map.md#rf) RF-012;\\n[ACT](fd-source-owner-map.md#act) §3/7;\\n[EVAL](fd-source-owner-map.md#eval) §4.\\n\\n### REQ-AC-FD-009 — Prepare independently acquirable review evidence\\n\\n**Input:** exact review claim/candidate and composition boundary, caller-selected\\nsource, comparison subjects, proof/evidence population and method-owned\\nindependence/exposure contract. **Output/checks:** independently resolvable raw\\nauthority/candidate/proof acquisition routes, acquired content where requested,\\nexact byte/record comparisons, and separate assertion/expected-result versus\\nexecution provenance. Support expectation recording before candidate exposure\\nand preserve the actual acquisition/exposure record under the supplied contract.\\nWorkers can acquire their implementation/proof context; Reviewers can inspect\\nthe actual candidate, tests/fixtures and source without author-only privileges.\\n**Limit:** diffs and trace/binding checks are not semantic findings, an independent\\nverdict or adoption of a review recommendation as disposition. Owners:\\n[EVAL](fd-source-owner-map.md#eval) §1–4/6;\\n[ASSURE](fd-source-owner-map.md#assure) §3/10/13–16;\\n[EXEC](fd-source-owner-map.md#exec) §9/10/17/19 if selected.\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[111,170]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"e3fcebd7e9fbc60dc36ed4c02ee834a96f14226af134809c938169d4712dfc23\",\"selected_sha256\":\"4cd8a5ffa6c769b503b8f017bfe15a0293278d0afce3406925a40e0433c3dd3e\",\"size_bytes\":3860,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"specification/requirements/fd-support-tools.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[111,170]},\"sha256\":\"e3fcebd7e9fbc60dc36ed4c02ee834a96f14226af134809c938169d4712dfc23\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:0a2e1c4b9b3baab54d1aade101c7344b04bf2f57d2a09fbb87da22f40925e25e","sha256":"0a2e1c4b9b3baab54d1aade101c7344b04bf2f57d2a09fbb87da22f40925e25e"},"id":"r-fdt-3","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=e05892e276837dc36c8793f7d862e627e53be8c9e38deabf8b2902207ec07546]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"invoked, bound to exact contract identity and decision authority. Report missing\nor mismatched required support before dispatch; retain draft and admitted\ncoordinates separately under the method's own contract. **Limit:** a successful\nshape/context check, role name, ticket state or tool invocation cannot mint\nadmission or work authority. The tool neither drafts a new grant nor admits the\nupstream outcome. Owners: [ACT](fd-source-owner-map.md#act) §1 Admission;\n[TICK](fd-source-owner-map.md#tick) §5.\n\n### REQ-AC-FD-007 — Dispatch, notify and observe under a supplied grant\n\n**Input:** exact preflighted activation/admission, selected executor operation,\nexisting grant, permitted tools/territory, material preconditions, effective\ncontext/settings and selected attempt/resource/observation conditions.\n**Output/checks:** invocation identity, actual supplied payload/settings,\nacknowledgments, output/partial-output and effect/termination observations with\nscope/time, retained attempts and decision-relevant return/exception/basis-change\nnotifications. Check material bindings before the named effect and expose\nchanged preconditions without silent rebase. **Limit:** the deterministic\nwrapper does not make F_P output deterministic or semantic evidence of success.\nRequests, delivery, evaluation, intended effects and their observed end remain\nseparate under the selected method; timeout/cancel/interruption preserve its\nunknown-effect semantics. Fallback observation is bounded by supplied conditions,\nnot a mandatory polling controller. Owners: [ACT](fd-source-owner-map.md#act)\n§1/3 Effects/5; [EXEC](fd-source-owner-map.md#exec) §6 if selected.\n\n### REQ-AC-FD-008 — Capture and check a closed return\n\n**Input:** returned payload/transport evidence, original activation and return\ncontract, expected consumer, exact subject/basis and supplied currentness,\ndependency and independence predicates/evidence. **Output/checks:** preserved raw\nreturn and provenance, deterministic binding/format/currentness findings and\nthe exact declared evaluations, predicates, domain outcomes and residuals that\nwere actually returned. Identify stale/wrong-subject/wrong-basis, missing,\nduplicate and conflicting evidence without dropping it; expose non-consumable\nsupport/gaps to the declared consumer. **Limit:** do not relabel a historical\nverdict as a new verdict, manufacture a result for an unperformed evaluation or\ntreat schema validity as semantic assessment/acceptance. A transport failure is\nreported separately using the selected method contract. Owners:\n[FOUND](fd-source-owner-map.md#found) Results/Conjunction of results;\n[RF](fd-source-owner-map.md#rf) RF-012;\n[ACT](fd-source-owner-map.md#act) §3/7;\n[EVAL](fd-source-owner-map.md#eval) §4.\n\n### REQ-AC-FD-009 — Prepare independently acquirable review evidence\n\n**Input:** exact review claim/candidate and composition boundary, caller-selected\nsource, comparison subjects, proof/evidence population and method-owned\nindependence/exposure contract. **Output/checks:** independently resolvable raw\nauthority/candidate/proof acquisition routes, acquired content where requested,\nexact byte/record comparisons, and separate assertion/expected-result versus\nexecution provenance. Support expectation recording before candidate exposure\nand preserve the actual acquisition/exposure record under the supplied contract.\nWorkers can acquire their implementation/proof context; Reviewers can inspect\nthe actual candidate, tests/fixtures and source without author-only privileges.\n**Limit:** diffs and trace/binding checks are not semantic findings, an independent\nverdict or adoption of a review recommendation as disposition. Owners:\n[EVAL](fd-source-owner-map.md#eval) §1–4/6;\n[ASSURE](fd-source-owner-map.md#assure) §3/10/13–16;\n[EXEC](fd-source-owner-map.md#exec) §9/10/17/19 if selected.\n\n","coordinates":{"lines":[111,170]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"e3fcebd7e9fbc60dc36ed4c02ee834a96f14226af134809c938169d4712dfc23","selected_sha256":"4cd8a5ffa6c769b503b8f017bfe15a0293278d0afce3406925a40e0433c3dd3e","size_bytes":3860,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"specification/requirements/fd-support-tools.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[111,170]},"sha256":"e3fcebd7e9fbc60dc36ed4c02ee834a96f14226af134809c938169d4712dfc23"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Y2AgUt6ECjRbzNoNDnyhBV","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAxngYKJsSaBF8FW4e54","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TSfajtXCUri6ZDsDTuKoBi","name":"mcp__ac_review__source_read","input":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"r-found-1","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"FOUNDATIONS.md","root":"method","selector":{"lines":[790,850]},"sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"encoding":"utf8","max_content_bytes":8192}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5855,"cache_read_input_tokens":77735,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5855},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9ee27ae-0996-4105-ba6f-30f3c0f28675","uuid":"b6cf467f-0f80-4ab6-958a-ea8556ae70b7","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:27:04.521Z","request_id":"req_011CgAxngHw26U8BQDeU2ffc","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01TSfajtXCUri6ZDsDTuKoBi":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"r-found-1","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"FOUNDATIONS.md","root":"method","selector":{"lines":[790,850]},"sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"encoding":"utf8","max_content_bytes":8192}}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TSfajtXCUri6ZDsDTuKoBi","display_name":"Source Read","server_display_name":"a_c.graphify.fd-support","tool_name":"source.read"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TSfajtXCUri6ZDsDTuKoBi","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:e3c24bd2e2d88cf369a162181b2678e0156648cae3c8e677d96bc512c89251e6\",\"sha256\":\"e3c24bd2e2d88cf369a162181b2678e0156648cae3c8e677d96bc512c89251e6\"},\"id\":\"r-found-1\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=f3fe5bcbea27c71a75f190d40cec1882da0aa22a04b99aa06b0c5b0140e4ddd1]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"### Results\\n\\nEvery performed evaluation returns one value of the core result algebra,\\ndirectly or as a refined value mapped into it (P5):\\n\\n| Value | Meaning |\\n|---|---|\\n| `satisfied` | the declared predicate holds on the exact basis |\\n| `falsified` | a declared counterexample defeats it |\\n| `indeterminate` | the available admissible evidence cannot decide it |\\n| `out_of_frame` | the evaluation requires an undeclared material relation or capability |\\n| `invalid_basis` | the subject or basis cannot support the evaluation |\\n\\nThis core is the only one. Results of constraints, judgments, frame\\nevaluations, stops, work steps and effects are stated in it or in a\\nrefinement mapped into it, so that results from any members combine under\\none rule ([Conjunction of results](#conjunction-of-results)). Purpose and\\nmaterial relation: no combination can report success while a failure, an\\nundecided question, an unperformed evaluation or an uncertain effect\\nremains, and none of these can be mistaken for another (P5, P6).\\n\\nRecording. A result records its core value together with the predicate\\nevaluated and the original domain outcome, which is the refined value\\nwhere a refinement produced it. A mapping into the core never owns domain\\nmeaning: the member, profile or adopting Product that defines the refined\\nvalue keeps it, and a consumer that needs the domain distinction reads the\\ndomain outcome, never the core value alone (P1, P6).\\n\\nStanding. The standing of a result is what it establishes about its\\npredicate; it is distinct from the standing of a commitment (§1). Only\\n`satisfied` establishes the predicate. `falsified` establishes that the\\npredicate fails and names the counterexample. `indeterminate`,\\n`out_of_frame` and `invalid_basis` establish neither, and each names what\\nwould decide: the evidence, the missing relation or capability with its\\nowner where the subject gives one, or the basis repair. By support for the\\npredicate, `satisfied` stands above each other value, and the other four\\nare not ordered among themselves.\\n\\nNo refinement or mapping raises a result's standing (P5, P6):\\n\\n- a falsified or failed result never maps to a satisfied or successful one;\\n- a result that admissible evidence cannot decide never maps to\\n  `satisfied`;\\n- an evaluation that was not performed stays distinct from one whose\\n  evidence cannot decide: it has no\\n  [closed result](ACTIVATION.md#7-closed-result-and-reuse), and it is never mapped\\n  to `indeterminate` or to any other core value;\\n- an effect whose completion is unknown never maps to no effect or to\\n  completed.\\n\\nNot performed. An evaluation that is required or planned and was not\\nperformed has no closed result; an actor cannot report an evaluation it\\ndid not perform (P6). Nothing is coerced to success: a failed,\\nindeterminate, out-of-frame, out-of-scope or invalid-basis result follows\\nthe declared result algebra and returns its own value under it, never\\n`satisfied`, and a missing result, being no result, enters every\\nconjunction over it as a gap: a planned assessment without a closed result\\nwhere an assessment was planned, and uncovered coverage where none was.\\nThis\\nconserves\\n[RF-012](stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.2/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME_METHOD.md#rf-012-closed-results),\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[790,850]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\",\"selected_sha256\":\"434abc238d13a2587a0d82146898a1328fe080c25618e42f03a4ba87e4d4ce15\",\"size_bytes\":3253,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[790,850]},\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9ee27ae-0996-4105-ba6f-30f3c0f28675","uuid":"8387ecea-1f44-475e-8c1d-a650a10595b4","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:27:04.716Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:e3c24bd2e2d88cf369a162181b2678e0156648cae3c8e677d96bc512c89251e6\",\"sha256\":\"e3c24bd2e2d88cf369a162181b2678e0156648cae3c8e677d96bc512c89251e6\"},\"id\":\"r-found-1\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=f3fe5bcbea27c71a75f190d40cec1882da0aa22a04b99aa06b0c5b0140e4ddd1]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"### Results\\n\\nEvery performed evaluation returns one value of the core result algebra,\\ndirectly or as a refined value mapped into it (P5):\\n\\n| Value | Meaning |\\n|---|---|\\n| `satisfied` | the declared predicate holds on the exact basis |\\n| `falsified` | a declared counterexample defeats it |\\n| `indeterminate` | the available admissible evidence cannot decide it |\\n| `out_of_frame` | the evaluation requires an undeclared material relation or capability |\\n| `invalid_basis` | the subject or basis cannot support the evaluation |\\n\\nThis core is the only one. Results of constraints, judgments, frame\\nevaluations, stops, work steps and effects are stated in it or in a\\nrefinement mapped into it, so that results from any members combine under\\none rule ([Conjunction of results](#conjunction-of-results)). Purpose and\\nmaterial relation: no combination can report success while a failure, an\\nundecided question, an unperformed evaluation or an uncertain effect\\nremains, and none of these can be mistaken for another (P5, P6).\\n\\nRecording. A result records its core value together with the predicate\\nevaluated and the original domain outcome, which is the refined value\\nwhere a refinement produced it. A mapping into the core never owns domain\\nmeaning: the member, profile or adopting Product that defines the refined\\nvalue keeps it, and a consumer that needs the domain distinction reads the\\ndomain outcome, never the core value alone (P1, P6).\\n\\nStanding. The standing of a result is what it establishes about its\\npredicate; it is distinct from the standing of a commitment (§1). Only\\n`satisfied` establishes the predicate. `falsified` establishes that the\\npredicate fails and names the counterexample. `indeterminate`,\\n`out_of_frame` and `invalid_basis` establish neither, and each names what\\nwould decide: the evidence, the missing relation or capability with its\\nowner where the subject gives one, or the basis repair. By support for the\\npredicate, `satisfied` stands above each other value, and the other four\\nare not ordered among themselves.\\n\\nNo refinement or mapping raises a result's standing (P5, P6):\\n\\n- a falsified or failed result never maps to a satisfied or successful one;\\n- a result that admissible evidence cannot decide never maps to\\n  `satisfied`;\\n- an evaluation that was not performed stays distinct from one whose\\n  evidence cannot decide: it has no\\n  [closed result](ACTIVATION.md#7-closed-result-and-reuse), and it is never mapped\\n  to `indeterminate` or to any other core value;\\n- an effect whose completion is unknown never maps to no effect or to\\n  completed.\\n\\nNot performed. An evaluation that is required or planned and was not\\nperformed has no closed result; an actor cannot report an evaluation it\\ndid not perform (P6). Nothing is coerced to success: a failed,\\nindeterminate, out-of-frame, out-of-scope or invalid-basis result follows\\nthe declared result algebra and returns its own value under it, never\\n`satisfied`, and a missing result, being no result, enters every\\nconjunction over it as a gap: a planned assessment without a closed result\\nwhere an assessment was planned, and uncovered coverage where none was.\\nThis\\nconserves\\n[RF-012](stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.2/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME_METHOD.md#rf-012-closed-results),\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[790,850]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\",\"selected_sha256\":\"434abc238d13a2587a0d82146898a1328fe080c25618e42f03a4ba87e4d4ce15\",\"size_bytes\":3253,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[790,850]},\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:e3c24bd2e2d88cf369a162181b2678e0156648cae3c8e677d96bc512c89251e6","sha256":"e3c24bd2e2d88cf369a162181b2678e0156648cae3c8e677d96bc512c89251e6"},"id":"r-found-1","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=f3fe5bcbea27c71a75f190d40cec1882da0aa22a04b99aa06b0c5b0140e4ddd1]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"### Results\n\nEvery performed evaluation returns one value of the core result algebra,\ndirectly or as a refined value mapped into it (P5):\n\n| Value | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `satisfied` | the declared predicate holds on the exact basis |\n| `falsified` | a declared counterexample defeats it |\n| `indeterminate` | the available admissible evidence cannot decide it |\n| `out_of_frame` | the evaluation requires an undeclared material relation or capability |\n| `invalid_basis` | the subject or basis cannot support the evaluation |\n\nThis core is the only one. Results of constraints, judgments, frame\nevaluations, stops, work steps and effects are stated in it or in a\nrefinement mapped into it, so that results from any members combine under\none rule ([Conjunction of results](#conjunction-of-results)). Purpose and\nmaterial relation: no combination can report success while a failure, an\nundecided question, an unperformed evaluation or an uncertain effect\nremains, and none of these can be mistaken for another (P5, P6).\n\nRecording. A result records its core value together with the predicate\nevaluated and the original domain outcome, which is the refined value\nwhere a refinement produced it. A mapping into the core never owns domain\nmeaning: the member, profile or adopting Product that defines the refined\nvalue keeps it, and a consumer that needs the domain distinction reads the\ndomain outcome, never the core value alone (P1, P6).\n\nStanding. The standing of a result is what it establishes about its\npredicate; it is distinct from the standing of a commitment (§1). Only\n`satisfied` establishes the predicate. `falsified` establishes that the\npredicate fails and names the counterexample. `indeterminate`,\n`out_of_frame` and `invalid_basis` establish neither, and each names what\nwould decide: the evidence, the missing relation or capability with its\nowner where the subject gives one, or the basis repair. By support for the\npredicate, `satisfied` stands above each other value, and the other four\nare not ordered among themselves.\n\nNo refinement or mapping raises a result's standing (P5, P6):\n\n- a falsified or failed result never maps to a satisfied or successful one;\n- a result that admissible evidence cannot decide never maps to\n  `satisfied`;\n- an evaluation that was not performed stays distinct from one whose\n  evidence cannot decide: it has no\n  [closed result](ACTIVATION.md#7-closed-result-and-reuse), and it is never mapped\n  to `indeterminate` or to any other core value;\n- an effect whose completion is unknown never maps to no effect or to\n  completed.\n\nNot performed. An evaluation that is required or planned and was not\nperformed has no closed result; an actor cannot report an evaluation it\ndid not perform (P6). Nothing is coerced to success: a failed,\nindeterminate, out-of-frame, out-of-scope or invalid-basis result follows\nthe declared result algebra and returns its own value under it, never\n`satisfied`, and a missing result, being no result, enters every\nconjunction over it as a gap: a planned assessment without a closed result\nwhere an assessment was planned, and uncovered coverage where none was.\nThis\nconserves\n[RF-012](stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.2/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME_METHOD.md#rf-012-closed-results),\n","coordinates":{"lines":[790,850]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f","selected_sha256":"434abc238d13a2587a0d82146898a1328fe080c25618e42f03a4ba87e4d4ce15","size_bytes":3253,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"FOUNDATIONS.md","root":"method","selector":{"lines":[790,850]},"sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TSfajtXCUri6ZDsDTuKoBi","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
