{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017hJ2Fv3jjJ58LN8tbfs376","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:531a147ff128ec0adf5c3e61d3dbfd4dc61b68b1f131e3524dfda4fc573db404\",\"sha256\":\"531a147ff128ec0adf5c3e61d3dbfd4dc61b68b1f131e3524dfda4fc573db404\"},\"id\":\"r-fdv-6\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=4e36978841d5aa4561ebee3c903182e706d04e8ad28aa1c605662749e8298850]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"| SC-AC-FD-008 Transport and uncertain effect | Distinguish receipt, schema-valid output, F_P return, observed effect and observed end. Lost response/timeout/cancel/interruption with partial write preserves upstream unknown-effect evidence and material retry preconditions. A termination request never proves completion/rollback. | FD-007,008,012,013; FDV-002 |\\n| SC-AC-FD-009 Closed return binding | Capture exact valid, stale, wrong-subject/basis, duplicate and conflicting returns. Preserve raw original predicates/domain outcomes; report consumer-binding errors and gaps without rewriting old verdicts, counting duplicate independence or fabricating unperformed results. | FD-008,010; FDV-002 |\\n| SC-AC-FD-010 Independent review acquisition | Under supplied exposure/independence conditions, record source-derived expectations before candidate exposure and permit a nonauthor Reviewer to acquire exact candidate, tests/fixtures, governing source and comparisons directly. Author summary/new session is not certified independent. The tool returns acquisition/diff facts, never review severity or disposition. | FD-003,005,009; FDV-001,002 |\\n| SC-AC-FD-011 Declared checks/conjunction | Execute a qualified supplied structural/proof predicate and method-owned operator. Preserve wrong-basis inputs, missing planned assessments, uncovered obligations, original domain outcomes and conflicts exactly. A necessary-condition pass cannot satisfy a stronger predicate; unsupported operations refuse. | FD-001,004,008,010; FDV-002 |\\n| SC-AC-FD-012 Existing state and authorized records | Project the named work/evidence carrier and apply one already-authorized actor/owner record through its Writer interface with preimage/grant checks. Preserve original ruling versus interpretation; a recommendation/commit/review event supplies no automatic disposition/closure/release, and generated views do not own work state. | FD-011; FDV-002 |\\n| SC-AC-FD-013 Refresh and fresh-actor handoff | Edit material source/frame inputs and compute affected support under supplied impact/reuse rules. Preserve originals/frozen studies and demonstrably valid survivors; incomplete dependencies leave uncertainty. A fresh actor resumes from current named sources without replay or blind retry of unreconciled effects. | FD-002,004,012; FDV-002 |\\n| SC-AC-FD-014 Notifications and resource evidence | Deliver return/exception/basis-change/checkpoint events and test declared bounded fallback when notifications fail. Retain failed/partial/retried attempts, units, unknown backend usage, elapsed versus summed intervals and selected limit checks without double counting or universal quotas. | FD-007,013; FDV-002 |\\n| SC-AC-FD-015 Matched usefulness | Compare matched tasks with/without support and retain bounded source/semantic/accepted-outcome and total cost evidence, including acquisition/authoring/refresh/repair/review and unknowns. Report actual results without extrapolating savings from fewer calls. | FD-013; FDV-003 |\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[76,84]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"3746e614a5ddc3f0a551e926998f16d6101cc037c5c43b879b4447b017a8dbdf\",\"selected_sha256\":\"1fecf891e0ba3300e1cb007eeaeba57c9ff182969825d5a3d3da96c76f2e9d79\",\"size_bytes\":3002,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"specification/requirements/fd-support-verification.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[76,84]},\"sha256\":\"3746e614a5ddc3f0a551e926998f16d6101cc037c5c43b879b4447b017a8dbdf\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9ee27ae-0996-4105-ba6f-30f3c0f28675","uuid":"e059bf83-4858-4285-98d6-e39f379d79fe","timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:27:34.202Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:531a147ff128ec0adf5c3e61d3dbfd4dc61b68b1f131e3524dfda4fc573db404\",\"sha256\":\"531a147ff128ec0adf5c3e61d3dbfd4dc61b68b1f131e3524dfda4fc573db404\"},\"id\":\"r-fdv-6\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=4e36978841d5aa4561ebee3c903182e706d04e8ad28aa1c605662749e8298850]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"| SC-AC-FD-008 Transport and uncertain effect | Distinguish receipt, schema-valid output, F_P return, observed effect and observed end. Lost response/timeout/cancel/interruption with partial write preserves upstream unknown-effect evidence and material retry preconditions. A termination request never proves completion/rollback. | FD-007,008,012,013; FDV-002 |\\n| SC-AC-FD-009 Closed return binding | Capture exact valid, stale, wrong-subject/basis, duplicate and conflicting returns. Preserve raw original predicates/domain outcomes; report consumer-binding errors and gaps without rewriting old verdicts, counting duplicate independence or fabricating unperformed results. | FD-008,010; FDV-002 |\\n| SC-AC-FD-010 Independent review acquisition | Under supplied exposure/independence conditions, record source-derived expectations before candidate exposure and permit a nonauthor Reviewer to acquire exact candidate, tests/fixtures, governing source and comparisons directly. Author summary/new session is not certified independent. The tool returns acquisition/diff facts, never review severity or disposition. | FD-003,005,009; FDV-001,002 |\\n| SC-AC-FD-011 Declared checks/conjunction | Execute a qualified supplied structural/proof predicate and method-owned operator. Preserve wrong-basis inputs, missing planned assessments, uncovered obligations, original domain outcomes and conflicts exactly. A necessary-condition pass cannot satisfy a stronger predicate; unsupported operations refuse. | FD-001,004,008,010; FDV-002 |\\n| SC-AC-FD-012 Existing state and authorized records | Project the named work/evidence carrier and apply one already-authorized actor/owner record through its Writer interface with preimage/grant checks. Preserve original ruling versus interpretation; a recommendation/commit/review event supplies no automatic disposition/closure/release, and generated views do not own work state. | FD-011; FDV-002 |\\n| SC-AC-FD-013 Refresh and fresh-actor handoff | Edit material source/frame inputs and compute affected support under supplied impact/reuse rules. Preserve originals/frozen studies and demonstrably valid survivors; incomplete dependencies leave uncertainty. A fresh actor resumes from current named sources without replay or blind retry of unreconciled effects. | FD-002,004,012; FDV-002 |\\n| SC-AC-FD-014 Notifications and resource evidence | Deliver return/exception/basis-change/checkpoint events and test declared bounded fallback when notifications fail. Retain failed/partial/retried attempts, units, unknown backend usage, elapsed versus summed intervals and selected limit checks without double counting or universal quotas. | FD-007,013; FDV-002 |\\n| SC-AC-FD-015 Matched usefulness | Compare matched tasks with/without support and retain bounded source/semantic/accepted-outcome and total cost evidence, including acquisition/authoring/refresh/repair/review and unknowns. Report actual results without extrapolating savings from fewer calls. | FD-013; FDV-003 |\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[76,84]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"3746e614a5ddc3f0a551e926998f16d6101cc037c5c43b879b4447b017a8dbdf\",\"selected_sha256\":\"1fecf891e0ba3300e1cb007eeaeba57c9ff182969825d5a3d3da96c76f2e9d79\",\"size_bytes\":3002,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"specification/requirements/fd-support-verification.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[76,84]},\"sha256\":\"3746e614a5ddc3f0a551e926998f16d6101cc037c5c43b879b4447b017a8dbdf\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:531a147ff128ec0adf5c3e61d3dbfd4dc61b68b1f131e3524dfda4fc573db404","sha256":"531a147ff128ec0adf5c3e61d3dbfd4dc61b68b1f131e3524dfda4fc573db404"},"id":"r-fdv-6","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=4e36978841d5aa4561ebee3c903182e706d04e8ad28aa1c605662749e8298850]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"| SC-AC-FD-008 Transport and uncertain effect | Distinguish receipt, schema-valid output, F_P return, observed effect and observed end. Lost response/timeout/cancel/interruption with partial write preserves upstream unknown-effect evidence and material retry preconditions. A termination request never proves completion/rollback. | FD-007,008,012,013; FDV-002 |\n| SC-AC-FD-009 Closed return binding | Capture exact valid, stale, wrong-subject/basis, duplicate and conflicting returns. Preserve raw original predicates/domain outcomes; report consumer-binding errors and gaps without rewriting old verdicts, counting duplicate independence or fabricating unperformed results. | FD-008,010; FDV-002 |\n| SC-AC-FD-010 Independent review acquisition | Under supplied exposure/independence conditions, record source-derived expectations before candidate exposure and permit a nonauthor Reviewer to acquire exact candidate, tests/fixtures, governing source and comparisons directly. Author summary/new session is not certified independent. The tool returns acquisition/diff facts, never review severity or disposition. | FD-003,005,009; FDV-001,002 |\n| SC-AC-FD-011 Declared checks/conjunction | Execute a qualified supplied structural/proof predicate and method-owned operator. Preserve wrong-basis inputs, missing planned assessments, uncovered obligations, original domain outcomes and conflicts exactly. A necessary-condition pass cannot satisfy a stronger predicate; unsupported operations refuse. | FD-001,004,008,010; FDV-002 |\n| SC-AC-FD-012 Existing state and authorized records | Project the named work/evidence carrier and apply one already-authorized actor/owner record through its Writer interface with preimage/grant checks. Preserve original ruling versus interpretation; a recommendation/commit/review event supplies no automatic disposition/closure/release, and generated views do not own work state. | FD-011; FDV-002 |\n| SC-AC-FD-013 Refresh and fresh-actor handoff | Edit material source/frame inputs and compute affected support under supplied impact/reuse rules. Preserve originals/frozen studies and demonstrably valid survivors; incomplete dependencies leave uncertainty. A fresh actor resumes from current named sources without replay or blind retry of unreconciled effects. | FD-002,004,012; FDV-002 |\n| SC-AC-FD-014 Notifications and resource evidence | Deliver return/exception/basis-change/checkpoint events and test declared bounded fallback when notifications fail. Retain failed/partial/retried attempts, units, unknown backend usage, elapsed versus summed intervals and selected limit checks without double counting or universal quotas. | FD-007,013; FDV-002 |\n| SC-AC-FD-015 Matched usefulness | Compare matched tasks with/without support and retain bounded source/semantic/accepted-outcome and total cost evidence, including acquisition/authoring/refresh/repair/review and unknowns. Report actual results without extrapolating savings from fewer calls. | FD-013; FDV-003 |\n\n","coordinates":{"lines":[76,84]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"3746e614a5ddc3f0a551e926998f16d6101cc037c5c43b879b4447b017a8dbdf","selected_sha256":"1fecf891e0ba3300e1cb007eeaeba57c9ff182969825d5a3d3da96c76f2e9d79","size_bytes":3002,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"specification/requirements/fd-support-verification.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[76,84]},"sha256":"3746e614a5ddc3f0a551e926998f16d6101cc037c5c43b879b4447b017a8dbdf"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017hJ2Fv3jjJ58LN8tbfs376","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
