edges or unaffectedness from absent paths, or treat schema/closure/size as semantic sufficiency.\n\nE2 implementation-conservation: code must realise the declared result algebra with exactly five core values; never raise standing (falsified->satisfied, undecidable->satisfied, not-performed->any value, unknown effect->none/completed) (FOUNDATIONS Results). Expected observable behaviours: FD001 unknown op/unsupported profile refuse with reason; FD002 dirty/untracked bytes detected without HEAD reliance; FD003 locator distinct from acquired content, missing/stale refs return gaps; FD005 no silent truncation, capacity measured only at declared boundary, unknown host context retained; FD006 preflight cannot mint admission from shape/role/ticket; FD007 request/delivery/effect/end separate, timeout/cancel preserve unknown effect, no silent rebase; FD008 raw return preserved, stale/wrong-subject/duplicate/conflicting detected, unperformed evaluations never fabricated, schema validity is not assessment; FD009 expectation recordable before candidate exposure, nonauthor direct candidate/test/source acquisition, diffs are not findings; FD010 joins only under supplied qualified operator, necessary-condition pass never full satisfaction; FD011 no rival ledger, no automatic adoption of recommendation, Reviewer/Executive mutation refused; FD012 history/frozen studies preserved, no unaffectedness inference; FD013 units/unknown counters/elapsed vs summed. ASSURANCE s11: proofs must acquire the owner-issued subject via the runnable surface, not a harness-reconstructed parallel state; where observation cannot separate subjects, indeterminate or narrower scope. Falsified by any demonstrated always-pass/always-refuse discriminator, standing raise, silent fallback/retry or rival owner semantics.\n\nE3 guide-task-criteria (TASK 1-6): LIFECYCLE_QUICKSTART.md <=140 lines Markdown; shows Executive discover/bind/handoff to a named granted Worker and independent Reviewer acquisition; >=1 concre